          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            %em general covariance
            is meant to indicate the property of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physical+system"} physical system
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+%28in+theoretical+physics%29"} model (in theoretical physics)
            whose
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space"} configurations
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
            are all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariance"} equivariant
            under the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism+group"} diffeomorphism group
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            underlying the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            or the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            of the system. Here “covariance” is as in “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+tensor"}> covariant tensor
            ” another term for behaviour under diffeomorphisms.
          %p
            The term
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+relativity"} general relativity
            for
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein"} Einstein
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            originates in at least closely related ideas (see
            %em
              %a{:href => "#HistoryAndOriginalFormulation"} History and original formulation
            below), and Einstein-gravity is the archtypical example of a generally covariant physical system:
          %p
            here, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space"} configuration space
            of physical fields over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            is not quite the space of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metrics"} Riemannian metrics
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            itself, but is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Fields
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Diff
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Sigma,\mathbf{Fields}]/\mathbf{Diff}(\Sigma)
            of this space by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism+group"} diffeomorphism group
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Diff
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Diff}(\Sigma)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_1
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_2
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            represent the same field of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            if there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism"} diffeomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi Σ
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : \Sigma \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} \Sigma
            such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_2 = f^* g_1
          %p
            Or rather, such a diffeomorphism is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+transformation"} gauge transformation
            between the two field configurations. The configuration space is not the naive
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
            of fields by diffeomorphisms as above, but is the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+quotient"} homotopy quotient
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+groupoid"} action groupoid
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Fields
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⫽
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Diff
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Sigma,\mathbf{Fields}]\sslash \mathbf{Diff}(\Sigma)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+cohesion"} infinitesimal approximation
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebroid"} Lie algebroid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BRST+complex"} BRST complex
            whose degree-1 elements are accordingly called the
            %em diffeomorphism ghosts
            (see there).
          %p
            As with all
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+transformations"} gauge transformations
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalent
            %em general covariance
            is an instance of the general
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principle+of+equivalence"} principle of equivalence
            in mathematics which says that sensible statements about
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            must respect the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
            and more general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalences"} equivalences
            between these objects.
          %p
            A physical system which is not generally covariant in this sense is hence one where the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            as above, underlying
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            is not regarded as modelling an absolute physical system (such as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observable+universe"} observable universe
            in gravity), but a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsystem"} subsystem
            that is equipped with ambient
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
            that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spontaneous+symmetry+breaking"} breaks
            the diffeomorphism symmetry. Notably systems like
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetism"} electromagnetism
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
            have traditionally been written in a non-generally covariant form describing gauge fields on a fixed gravitational background, as for instance the space inhabited by a particle accelerator. This ambient structure on the spacetime
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            breaks its general diffeomorphism invariance and hence the effective resulting theory on this background is not generally covariant (a special case of the general phenomenon of
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spontaneous+symmetry+breaking"} spontaneous symmetry breaking
          %p
            On the other hand, such a model consisting of background (e.g. the particle accelerator) and quantum fields propagating in it is ultimately to be understood as an approximation to a more encompassing model in which also the background is dynamical, and which is again generally covariant. Specific for electromagnetism and Yang-Mills theory this refined generally covariant model is known as
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein-Maxwell+theory"} Einstein-Maxwell theory
            or more generally
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein-Yang-Mills+theory"} Einstein-Yang-Mills theory
          %p
            The idea of general covariance has a long and convoluted history and the literature witnesses plenty of disagreement about how to interpret and formalize it in technical detail (
            %a{:href => "#Norton"}> Norton
            ). Already early arguments by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein"} Einstein
            himself (e.g. the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hole+paradox"}> hole paradox
            ” (
            %a{:href => "#EinsteinGrossmann"}> Einstein-Grossmann
            )) show that the discussion has suffered from the beginning from lack of the basic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theoretic
            concept of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"} Diff
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            %em
              %a{:href => "#InHomotopyTypeTheory"} Formalization in homotopy type theory
            we indicate a formalization of general covariance that is general, fundamental, and accurately reflects the role of the term in theoretical physics.
          %h2#HistoryAndOriginalFormulation History and original formulation
          %blockquote
            %p
              The question of general covariance of physical theories in space and time can be traced back to the famous debate between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gottfried+Wilhelm+Leibniz"} Gottfried Wilhelm Leibniz
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Samuel+Clarke"} Samuel Clarke
              (the latter assisted by Sir
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isaac+Newton"} Isaac Newton
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ontology"} ontological
              status of space in the years 1715–1716 (
              %a{:href => "#Alexander"}> Alexander
              ), the central question being if space exists as a substance or as an absolute being and absolute motion is present (Clarke) or if it is constituted only in relation to co-existent things allowing for relativism in motions only (Leibniz). This kind of problems also played an important role when the general theory of relativity was being developed in the years around 1910. While
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Albert+Einstein"} Albert Einstein
              first characterized generally covariant field equations as inadmissible since they did not determine the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metric"} metric field
              uniquely as shown in the hole argument (
              %em Lochbetrachtung
              ) in the appendix of (
              %a{:href => "#EinsteinGrossmann"}> Einstein-Grossmann
              ), he later accepted (
              %a{:href => "#Einstein1916"}> Einstein 1916
              ) that all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physical+laws"} physical laws
              had to be expressed by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations"} equations
              that are valid in all
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate+systems"} coordinate systems
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/substitution"} substitutions
            %blockquote
              %p
                %em Die allgemeinen Naturgesetze sind durch Gleichungen auszudrücken, die für alle Koordinatensysteme gelten, d. h. die beliebigen Substitutionen gegenüber kovariant (allgemein kovariant) sind.
                (
                %a{:href => "#Einstein1916"}> Einstein 1916 p. 776
                )
            %p
              The hole argument was dismissed by the reasoning that it is not the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metric"} metric
              that has to be fixed uniquely by the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} field equations
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurement"} measurements
              result in statements on meetings of material points of the measuring rods with other material points or in coincidences between watch hands and points on the clockface. The introduction of a reference system merely serves the easy description of the totality of all these coincidences (point-coincidence argument) (
              %a{:href => "#Einstein1916"}> Einstein 1916 p. 776f
              ).
            %p
              from (
              %a{:href => "#BrunettiPorrmannRuzzi"}> Brunetti-Pormann-Ruzzi
              )
          %h2#ModernFormulationInDifferentialGeometry Modern formulation in differential geometry
          %p
            We discuss the modern formulation of general covariance in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometry
          %h3#in_gravity In gravity
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ∈
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma \in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SmoothMfd"} SmoothMfd
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Riem
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Riem(\Sigma)
            for the space of (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-Riemannian+metric"}> pseudo
            \-)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metrics"} Riemannian metrics
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo →
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : \Sigma \to \Sigma
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism"} diffeomorphism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %mi Riem
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Riem
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^* : Riem(\Sigma) \to Riem(\Sigma)
            which sends a Riemannian metric to its pullback:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi v
                  %mo ,
                  %mi w
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mi v
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mi w
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (f^*g)(v,w) \coloneqq g(f_* v, f_* w)
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %mi T
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo →
                  %mi T
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_* : T\Sigma \to T\Sigma
            is the canonical map induced on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
            (see at
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivative"} derivative
          %p
            Say that two metrics
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_1, g_2
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+transformation"} gauge equivalent
            if there is a diffeomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_2 = f^* g_1
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Riem
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi Diff
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Riem(\Sigma)/Diff(\Sigma)
            for the corresponding set of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+classes"} equivalence classes
          %p
            The statement of
            %em general covariance
            is that the distinct configurations of the gravitational field form the set
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Riem
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi Diff
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Riem(\Sigma)/Diff(\Sigma)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein-Hilbert+action"} Einstein-Hilbert action
            functional which
            %em a priori
            is defined on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Riem
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Riem(\Sigma)
            descends to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Riem
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi Diff
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Riem(\Sigma)/Diff(\Sigma)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi EH
                  %mo :
                  %mi Riem
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi Diff
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  S_{EH} : Riem(\Sigma)/Diff(\Sigma) \to \mathbb{R}
                  \\,.
          %p
            While this captures the idea of general covariance accurately, for further development of the theory of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Riem
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi Diff
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Riem(\Sigma)/Diff(\Sigma)
            needs to be refined. It is really equipped with the structure of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+space"} smooth space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Riem
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Diff
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Riem}(\Sigma)/\mathbf{Diff}(\Sigma)
            (in order to perform
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variational+calculus"} variational calculus
            and hence derive the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
            of the theory), and second it is to be refined to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+infinity-groupoid"} smooth groupoid
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Riem
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⫽
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Diff
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Riem}(\Sigma)\sslash\mathbf{Diff}(\Sigma)
          %p
            Finally, for setups that admit to introduce
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fermions"} fermions
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinors"} spinors
            into the model one needs to refine Riemannian metrics to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vielbein"} vielbein
            fields/
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+structures"}> orthogonal structures
            \. The fully refined generally covariance smooth configuration groupoid is then
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi orth
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⫽
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Diff
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Sigma, \mathbf{orth}]\sslash \mathbf{Diff}(\Sigma)
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#GravityInHoTT"} below
          %h3#RelationToPrincipleOfEquivalenceInGravity Relation to the “principle of equivalence” in gravity
          %p
            The
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+principle+%28physics%29"} principle of equivalence
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+relativity"} general relativity
            is formally the statement that around every point in a (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-Riemannian+metric"}> pseudo
            \-)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+manifold"} Riemannian manifold
            one can find a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate+system"} coordinate system
            such that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Levi-Civita+connection"} Levi-Civita connection
            vanishes (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+normal+coordinates"}> Riemann normal coordinates
            ”), which means that to
            %strong
              first
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+space"} infinitesimal
              order
            around that point particle dynamics subject to the force of gravity is equivalent to dynamics in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            with vanishing field of gravity.
          %p
            By the above, this is a special case of the principle of general covariance: for every field configuration
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            and every given point there is a gauge equivalent field configuration
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^* g
            such that the “force of gravity” (the Levi-Civita connection) vanishes at that point.
          %p
            It is via this relation that the physical “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+principle+%28physics%29"}> principle of equivalence
            ” relates to the mathematical
            = succeed ":" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principle+of+equivalence"} principle of equivalence
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+transformation"} gauge transformation
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principle+of+equivalence"} principle of equivalence
            in mathematics
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⇒
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Rightarrow
            principle of general covariance
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⇒
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Rightarrow
            principle of equivalence in physics .
          %h3#in_other_topological_field_theories In other topological field theories
          %h2#InHomotopyTypeTheory Formalization in homotopy type theory
          %p
            We discuss here that general covariance in field theory has a natural formalization in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+field+theory"} classical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            in this fashion see (
            %a{:href => "#SchreiberLectures"}> Schreiber, ESI lectures
            ) and (
            %a{:href => "#SchreiberShulman"}> Schreiber-Shulman
            ).
          %p
            The same kind of construction yields important
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stacks"} moduli stacks
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack+of+Riemann+surfaces"} moduli stack of Riemann surfaces
            %a{:href => "moduli+space+of+curves#InTermsOfTheHigherToposOfSmoothStacks"} this remark
            there.
          %h3#InformalIntroduction Informal introduction
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            to be thought of as
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
          %p
            Then the central idea of
            %em general covariance
            is that for
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi i
                    %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi U
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  i_1 \;\colon\; U \hookrightarrow \Sigma
          %p and
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi i
                    %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi U
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  i_2 \;\colon\; U \hookrightarrow \Sigma
          %p
            two
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsets"} subsets
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submanifolds"} submanifolds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalent
            if there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism"} diffeomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Σ
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \;\colon\; \Sigma \stackrel{}{\longrightarrow} \Sigma
            which takes one to the other, hence such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_2 = \phi^\ast i_1 \coloneqq\phi \circ i_1
          %p
            That this statement can be puzzling if one thinks of the case
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo =
                  %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U = \ast
            as being just a single point is the content of the historical “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hole+argument"} hole argument
            = succeed "\u201D." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paradox"} paradox
          %p
            But with just a little bit of formalization the apparent paradox is resolved, because the above evidently just says that the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space"}> moduli space
            ” for “subsets of spacetime” is not the manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            itself, but is rather a “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"}> moduli stack
            ” namely the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+stack"} quotient stack
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi Diff
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma //Diff(\Sigma)
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism+group"} diffeomorphism group
          %p
            Indeed, the technical term “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+stack"}> quotient stack
            ” is precisely defined by the condition that for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            of the shape of a
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disk"} disk
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate+chart"} coordinate chart
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi U
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ⫽
                  %mi Diff
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  i \;\colon\; U \hookrightarrow \Sigma \longrightarrow \Sigma \sslash Diff(\Sigma)
          %p to it are equivalent if (and only if) there is a diffeomorphism relating them, as above.
          %p
            So if in a generally covariant field theory spacetime is not actually the manifold
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ⫽
                    %mi Diff
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma \sslash Diff(\Sigma)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} field
            in this generally covariant field theory should be a field on that quotient stack, not on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            itself.
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Fields
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Fields}
            a
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space"} moduli space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} fields
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Φ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Fields
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Phi \;\colon\; \Sigma \longrightarrow \mathbf{Fields}
          %p
            and accordingly the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space"} space of all field configurations
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+space"} mapping space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Fields
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Sigma, \mathbf{Fields}]
          %p From this it is clear that for a generally covariant field theory we are instead to declare that the space of field configurations is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ⫽
                  %mi Diff
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Fields
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [\Sigma \sslash Diff(\Sigma), \;\mathbf{Fields}]
                  \\,.
          %p
            And it is at this point that
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-topos+theory"} higher topos theory
            works a little wonder for us – namely it provides proof – and this is what is discussed below – that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ⫽
                  %mi Diff
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Fields
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ≃
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Fields
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ⫽
                  %mi Diff
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [\Sigma \sslash Diff(\Sigma),\; \mathbf{Fields}]
                  \\simeq
                  [\Sigma,\; \mathbf{Fields}] \sslash Diff(\Sigma)
                  \\,.
          %p
            In words, the right hand side is the time-honored answer: two fields
            %em on
            a spacetime manifold
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+equivalence"} gauge equivalent
            %em in
            spacetime are to be equivalent if related by a diffeomorphism.
          %p
            Here to read the above equivalence as a theorem, we have to read the left hand side, as it should, be “in the context of
            = succeed "-actions\u201D." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Diff
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Diff(\Sigma)
            = succeed "-dependence" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/context"} context
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            takes care of, and this is what the following technical statement deals with.
          %h3#introduction_in_terms_of_type_theory Introduction in terms of type theory
          %p
            A basic idea of traditional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            is of course that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/types"} types
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            may appear
            %em
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/context"} context
            of other types
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi Type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  x : \Gamma \vdash A(x) : Type
          %p
            is that of a
            = succeed "-parameterized" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle"} bundle
            of types, whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in \Gamma
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A(x)
          %p
            But in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+types"} homotopy types
            and, hence so are the contexts. A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+in+context"} type in context
            is now in general something more refined than just a family of types. It is really a family of types equipped with
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariance"} equivariance
            structure with respect to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
            of the context type.
          %p
            Hence in homotopy theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/types+in+context"} types in context
            generically satisfy an
            = succeed "-principle." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariance"} equivariance
          %p
            Specifically, if the context type is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-connected+object+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} connected
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+object"} pointed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo ≃
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \simeq \mathbf{B}G
            of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group"} ∞-group
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-action"} ∞-action
            – that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/context"} context
            defined by the type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            is that of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariance"} equivariance
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-action"} ∞-action
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "-actions" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %em
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/context"} context
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
          %p
            In the following we discuss this for the case that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+%E2%88%9E-group"} automorphism ∞-group
            of a type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            which is regarded as representing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            or a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Fields
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Fields}
            a moduli object for the given fields, so that a field configuration is a function
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo :
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Fields
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi : \Sigma \to \mathbf{Fields}
            %em covariant
            fields is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+type"} function type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Fields
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Sigma \to \mathbf{Fields})
            but formed in the “general covariance context”
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}\mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} interpreted
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+infinity-groupoid"} smooth models
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Conf
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Conf}
            is the smooth groupoid of field configurations and diffeomorphism gauge transformations acting on them, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integrations
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BRST+complex"} BRST complex
            whose degree-1 elements are the
            = succeed "." do
              %em diffeomorphism ghosts
          %p More precisely, we show the following.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              Consider in homotopy type theory two types
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo ,
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Fields
                      %mo :
                      %mi Type
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vdash \Sigma, \mathbf{Fields} : Type
              %em spacetime
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %em field moduli
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi Type
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\vdash \mathbf{B}\mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma) : Type
            %p
              be the image of the name of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo :
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\vdash \Sigma : \mathbf{B}\mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Perform the canonical context extension of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              and trivial context extension of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Fields
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Fields}
              to get types in context
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo :
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo :
                    %mi Type
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Sigma : \mathbf{B}\mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma)
                    \\vdash
                    \\Sigma : Type
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo :
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Fields
                    %mo :
                    %mi Type
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Sigma : \mathbf{B}\mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma)
                    \\vdash
                    \\mathbf{Fields} : Type
                    \\,.
            %p Form then the type of field moduli
            %p
              “
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Conf
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Fields
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Conf} \coloneqq (\Sigma \to \mathbf{Fields})
              ”
            %p
              %em> in this context
              \:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Conf
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo :
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Fields
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi Type
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{Conf} \coloneqq
                    \\;\;\;\;\;
                    \\Sigma : \mathbf{B}\mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma)
                    \\vdash (\Sigma \to \mathbf{Fields}) : Type
                    \\,.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Conf
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Conf}
              in the model
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Smooth∞Grpd
              of the homotopy type theory, and for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ∈
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma \in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SmoothMfd"} SmoothMfd
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi Smooth
                      %mn ∞
                      %mi Grpd
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hookrightarrow Smooth \infty Grpd
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+space"} diffeological groupoid
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Conf
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Fields
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⫽
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Diff
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{Conf}
                    \=
                    [\Sigma, \mathbf{Fields}]\sslash \mathbf{Diff}(\Sigma)
            %p
              whose objects are field configurations on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              and whose morphisms are diffeomorphism gauge transformations between them. In particular the corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebroid"} Lie algebroid
              is dual to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BRST+complex"} BRST complex
              of fields with diffeomorphism ghosts in degree 1.
          %h3#the_ambient_theory The ambient theory
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            for the ambient
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} interpretation
            given by an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            we have
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H} =
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Smooth∞Grpd
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SmoothSuper%E2%88%9EGrpd"} SmoothSuper∞Grpd
            or similar, but none of the following general discussion depends on a concrete choice for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
          %p
            Pick once and for all an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ∈
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Sigma \in \mathbf{H}
          %p
            supposed to represent the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
            underlying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            or the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+%28in+theoretical+physics%29"} model (in theoretical physics)
          %h3#the_diffeomorphism_group The diffeomorphism group
          %p Write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Grp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma) \in Grp(\mathbf{H})
          %p
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+%E2%88%9E-group"} automorphism ∞-group
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space+object"} loop space object
            of the
            = succeed "-factorization" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+image"} homotopy image
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo *
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi Σ
                  %mi Type
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  * \stackrel{\vdash \Sigma}{\to} Type
                  \\,,
          %p
            hence the factorization by an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+epimorphism+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} effective epimorphism
            followed by a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} monomorphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo *
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo ↪
                    %mrow
                  %mi Type
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  * \stackrel{}{\to} \mathbf{B}\mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma)
                  \\stackrel{}{\hookrightarrow} Type
                  \\,.
          %p
            In the standard
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} interpretation
            of the homotopy type theory in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H} =
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Smooth∞Grpd
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            could be an ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            or
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold"} orbifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Diff
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma) = \mathbf{\Diff}(\Sigma)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism+group"} diffeomorphism group
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+space"} diffeological
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+object"} group object
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism"} diffeomorphism
            for short instead of
            %em
              auto-equivalence in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            and similarly refer to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma)
            loosely as the
            %em diffeomorphism group
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H} =
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Smooth∞Grpd
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SmoothSuper%E2%88%9EGrpd"} SmoothSuper∞Grpd
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            can be much more general than a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifold"} supermanifold
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold"} orbifold
          %h3#the_context_of_general_covariance The context of general covariance
          %p
            Write then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B} \mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma) \in \mathbf{H}
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            of the diffeomorphism group. The essentially unique
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/term"} term
            of this type is to be thought of as being
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            itself, and so we write it as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\vdash \Sigma : \mathbf{B} \mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma)
                  \\,.
          %p
            By the discussion at
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-action"} ∞-action
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+in+context"} type in context
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}\mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Sigma : \mathbf{B} \mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma) \vdash V(\Sigma)
          %p
            is a type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mi V
                  %mo :
                  %mi Type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vdash V : Type
            in the absolute context equipped with an
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-action"} ∞-action
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo :
                  %mi V
                  %mo ×
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho : V \times \mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma) \to V
            on it. The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+sum"} dependent sum
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊢
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo :
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Aut
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi Type
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\vdash \sum_{\Sigma : \mathbf{B}\mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma)} V(\Sigma) : Type
                  \\,,
          %p which we also write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo ⫽
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo :
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Aut
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  V \sslash \mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma)
                  \\coloneqq
                  \\sum_{\Sigma : \mathbf{B}\mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma)}
                  V(\Sigma)
                  \\,,
          %p
            is the total space of the universal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} associated
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} fiber ∞-bundle
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi V
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                            %mrow
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi Aut
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi Σ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi V
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Σ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mover
                              %mi ρ
                              %mo ¯
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi Aut
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Σ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  V &amp;\to&amp; \sum_{\mathbf{B}\mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma)} V(\Sigma)
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\overline{\rho}}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}\mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma)
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            Hence the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} interpretation
            of the context
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma : \mathbf{B}\mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} slice (∞,1)-topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Aut
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}_{/\mathbf{B}\mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma)}
            and equivalently is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            of objects in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            equipped with
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-actions"} ∞-actions
            and of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariance"} equivariant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            between them:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Aut
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi Act
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{H}_{/\mathbf{B}\mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma)}
                  \\simeq
                  Act_{\mathbf{H}}(\mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma))
                  \\,.
          %p
            Hence a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+in+context"} type in context
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma : \mathbf{B}\mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma)
            is a “generally covariant type” with respect to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            in the sense that it transforms
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+functor"} covariantly
            by equivalences under diffeomorphisms of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
          %p
            %strong Fact.
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma : \mathbf{B}\mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma)
            %em
              is the
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/context"} context
                of general covariance
              with respect to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
          %p In the precise formal sense.
          %p
            In particular,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            itself is canonically equipped with the defining action of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma)
            on it, which
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/syntax"} syntactically
            we may write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo :
                  %mi Type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Sigma : \mathbf{B}\mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma) \vdash \Sigma : Type
          %p
            and which
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} semantically
            is exhibited by the universal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} associated
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} fiber ∞-bundle
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Σ
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                            %mrow
                              %mi Σ
                              %mo :
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi Aut
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi Σ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi Σ
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mover
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi ρ
                                  %mi Σ
                              %mo ¯
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi Aut
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Σ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\Sigma &amp;\to&amp; \sum_{\Sigma : \mathbf{B}\mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma)} \Sigma
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\overline{\rho_{\Sigma}}}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B} \mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma)
                  }
                  \\,,
          %p
            given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universe"} universe
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi Type
                    %mo ˜
                  %mo →
                  %mi Type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widetilde Type \to Type
            along the defining
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} inclusion
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Aut
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Type
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}\mathbf{Aut} \hookrightarrow Type
          %p Here the total space
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ⫽
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo :
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Aut
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Sigma \sslash \mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma)
                  \\coloneqq
                  \\sum_{\Sigma : \mathbf{B}\mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma) } \Sigma
          %p
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+quotient"} homotopy quotient
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+groupoid"} action groupoid
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi U
                  %mo →
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ⫽
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : U \to \Sigma \sslash \mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma)
            is a function to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            which is regarded as (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+equivalence"}> gauge
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalent
            to another function to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            if both differ by postcomposition with a diffeomorphism of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
          %h3#generally_covariant_field_configuration_spaces Generally covariant field configuration spaces
          %p Let now
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Fields
                  %mo ∈
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{Fields} \in \mathbf{H}
          %p
            be an object that represents the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+%E2%88%9E-stack"} moduli ∞-stack
            of field configurations on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            for some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+%28in+theoretical+physics%29"} model (in theoretical physics)
            to be described. For instance for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Grp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \in Grp(\mathbf{H})
            an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group"} ∞-group
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+homotopy+type+theory"} cohesive homotopy type theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Fields
                  %mo =
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi conn
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Fields} = \mathbf{B}G_{conn}
            the moduli for a choice of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+an+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} principal ∞-connection
            = succeed "-(" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+gauge+theory"} higher
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+fields"} gauge fields
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Fields
                  %mo =
                  %mi X
                  %mo ∈
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Fields} = X \in \mathbf{H}
            we may always regard
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target space
            of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
          %p
            Then the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Fields
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Fields
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ∈
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{Fields}(\Sigma) \coloneqq [\Sigma, \mathbf{Fields}] \in \mathbf{H}
          %p
            hence the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+type"} function type
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Fields
                  %mo :
                  %mi Type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\vdash \Sigma \to \mathbf{Fields} : Type
          %p
            is the
            %em naive
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space"} configuration space
            of the model. This is not generally covariant, precisely so by the above definition: it is not in the generally covariant context
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi Aut
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}_{/\mathbf{B} \mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma)}
          %p
            But by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+image"} inverse image
            of the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}\mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+product"} dependent product
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+geometric+morphism"} étale geometric morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi G
                  %mover
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %munder
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                            %mrow
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi Aut
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi Σ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                          %mrow
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi Aut
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Σ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{H}_{/\mathbf{B}G}
                  \\stackrel{\overset{\sum_{\mathbf{B}\mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma)}}{\to}}{
                  \\stackrel{\overset{}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{\prod_{\mathbf{B}\mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma)}}{\to}}}
                  \\mathbf{H}
          %p
            which is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/context+enlargement"} context enlargement
            by
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}\mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Fields
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Fields}
            is freely moved to the general covariant context, where it is regarded as equipped with the
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "infinity-action#TrivialAction"} trivial ∞-action
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Fields
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Aut
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Fields} \in \mathbf{H}_{/\mathbf{B}\mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma)}
            with that trivial action understood, which is justified by the precise syntactic expression for it:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Fields
                  %mo :
                  %mi Type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Sigma : \mathbf{B}\mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma) \vdash \mathbf{Fields} : Type
          %p
            We may then form the
            %em configuration space of fields in the generally covariant context
            \. As before, a field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
            should be a function on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            with values in the moduli type of field configurations, but now we interpret this statement in the generally covariant context. Syntactically this simply means that a field is now a term in
            = succeed "-context" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}\mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo :
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Fields
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Sigma : \mathbf{B}\mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma)
                  \\vdash
                  \\phi : \Sigma \to \mathbf{Fields}
          %p and that accordingly the configuration space of fields is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Fields
                  %mo :
                  %mi Type
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Sigma : \mathbf{B}\mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma)
                  \\vdash
                  \\Sigma \to \mathbf{Fields} : Type
                  \\,.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} semantics
            of this is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
            in the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} slice (∞,1)-topos
            %em
              %a{:href => "infinity-action#CartesianClosedMonoidalStructure"} Internal hom of ∞-actions
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Conf
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ⫽
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Fields
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Aut
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{Conf}
                  \\coloneqq
                  [\Sigma \sslash \mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma), \mathbf{Fields}]
                  \\in
                  \\mathbf{H}_{/\mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma)}
                  \\,,
          %p
            The central observation now is that discussed at
            = succeed ":" do
              %em
                %a{:href => "infinity-action#GeneralCovariance"} ∞-action – Examples – General covariance
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Conf
                  %mo ≃
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Fields
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ⫽
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{Conf} \simeq [\Sigma,\mathbf{Fields}] \sslash \mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma)
          %p
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+quotient"} homotopy quotient
            of the naive fields
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∈
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Fields
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \in \mathbf{Fields}(\Sigma)
            by the action of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism+group"} diffeomorphism group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+equivalence"} gauge equivalence
            between any two field configurations that differ after pullback along a diffeomorphism.
          %p This is precisely as it should be for configuration space of generally covariant theories. We have found:
          %p
            %strong> Fact
            \. In terms of homotopy type theory, configuration spaces of a generally covariant theory over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            are precisely the ordinary configuration spaces of fields, but formed in the context
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}\mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Conf
                  %msub
                    %mo =
                    %mi def
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Field
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi Type
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{Conf} =_{def}
                  \\;\;\;\;\;\;
                  \\Sigma : \mathbf{B}\mathbf{Aut}(\Sigma) \vdash (\Sigma \to \mathbf{Field}) : Type
                  \\,.
          %h3#GravityInHoTT Generally covariant field of gravity
          %p
            We now spell out the example of ordinary
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein"} Einstein
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            in this language. Plenty of further examples work analogously.
          %p
            For pure
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H} =
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Smooth∞Grpd
            or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} =
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SynthDiff%E2%88%9EGrpd"} SynthDiff∞Grpd
          %p
            If we denote by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mi n
                  %mo ∈
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D^n \in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SynthDiff%E2%88%9EGrpd"} SynthDiff∞Grpd
            the first order
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+object"} infinitesimal neighbourhood
            of the origin in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  GL(n) = \mathbf{Aut}(D^n)
          %p
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+%E2%88%9E-group"} automorphism ∞-group
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D^n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}GL(n)
            as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊢
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mi n
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\vdash D^n : \mathbf{B}GL(n)
                  \\,.
          %p
            The fields of Einstein gravity are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+structures"} orthogonal structures
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metrics"}> Riemannian metrics
            ) on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ∈
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma \in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SmoothMfd"} SmoothMfd
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ↪
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hookrightarrow \mathbf{H}
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+structure"} orthogonal structure
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vielbein"} vielbein
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/context"} context
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+linear+group"} general linear group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Grp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n) \in Grp(\mathbf{H})
            via its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo →
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \Sigma \to \Sigma
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            to which the tangent bundle is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+bundle"} associated
          %p
            By the discussion at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} principal ∞-bundle
            this is modulated by a morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi T
                      %mi Σ
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi GL
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\Sigma \stackrel{\vdash T \Sigma}{\to} \mathbf{B} GL(n))
                  \\in
                  \\mathbf{H}_{/\mathbf{B} GL(n)}
          %p
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}GL(n)
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n)
            (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n)
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundles"} principal bundles
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+sequence"} fiber sequence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi T
                          %mi Σ
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi Σ
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mo ⊢
                                %mi T
                                %mi Σ
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi GL
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  T \Sigma &amp;\to&amp; \Sigma
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\vdash T \Sigma}}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}GL(n)
                  }
          %p
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            = succeed ").)" do
              %a{:href => "#SchreiberLectures"} Schreiber, ESI lectures
          %p
            Therefore the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/syntax"} syntax
            of the tangent bundle as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type"} dependent type
            is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mi n
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mi T
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi Type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  D^n : \mathbf{B}GL(n) \vdash T \Sigma(D^n) : Type
          %p
            and since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D^n
            is essentially unique we will notationally suppress it in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/succedent"} succedent
            on the right and just write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mi n
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mi T
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo :
                  %mi Type
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  D^n : \mathbf{B}GL(n) \vdash T \Sigma : Type
                  \\,.
          %p Let then
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi orth
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi GL
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\mathbf{B} O(n) \stackrel{\mathbf{orth}}{\to} \mathbf{B} GL(n))
                  \\in
                  \\mathbf{H}_{/\mathbf{B}GL(n)}
          %p
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            of the inclusion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(n) \to GL(n)
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maximal+compact+subgroup"} maximal compact subgroup
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+group"} orthogonal group
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(n)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice-%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} slice-(∞,1)-topos
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}GL(n)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber+sequence"} homotopy fiber sequence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi GL
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi O
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi O
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi orth
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi GL
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  GL(n)/O(n) &amp;\to&amp; \mathbf{B}O(n)
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{orth}}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}GL(n)
                  }
          %p
            with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coset"} coset
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+space"} smooth space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n)/O(n)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/syntax"} syntax
            of this object is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type"} dependent type
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mi n
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi Type
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  D^n : \mathbf{B}GL(n) \vdash GL(n)/O(n) : Type
                  \\,.
          %p
            In view of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} equivalence of (∞,1)-categories
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi GL
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi Act
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{H}_{/\mathbf{B}GL(n)} \simeq Act_{\mathbf{H}}(GL(n))
          %p
            this expresses the canonical
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-action"} action
            on the coset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n)/O(n)
            (by mutliplication from the “other side”).
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/syntax"} syntax
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vielbein"} vielbein
            fields /
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metrics"} Riemannian metrics
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊢
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi D
                        %mi n
                      %mo :
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi GL
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi T
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo →
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi Type
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\vdash \prod_{D^n : \mathbf{B}GL(n)} T \Sigma \to GL(n)/O(n) : Type
                  \\,.
          %p This almost verbatim expresses the familiar statement:
          %blockquote
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vielbein"} vielbein
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              is a
              = succeed "-equivariant" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi GL
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \Sigma
              to the coset
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi GL
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi O
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n)/O(n)
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            of such a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vielbein"} vielbein
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
            is as a diagram
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Σ
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi O
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ⇙
                            %mi e
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ↙
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi orth
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi GL
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\Sigma &amp;&amp; \stackrel{}{\to}&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}O(n)
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \searrow &amp;\swArrow_{e}&amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{orth}}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}GL(n)
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p This in turn almost verbatim expresses the familar equivalent statement
          %blockquote
            %p
              A vielbein is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduction+of+the+structure+group"} reduction of the structure group
              of the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi GL
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \Sigma
              along
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi O
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi GL
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(n) \to GL(n)
          %p
            This is still the naive space of fields, not yet generally covariant. So we next pass to the general covariant
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}\mathbf{Aut}(T\Sigma)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/context"} context
            and form the correct generally covariant space of fields, being the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+in+context"} type in context
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B} \mathbf{Aut}(T \Sigma)
            given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Conf
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo ⊢
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi D
                        %mi n
                      %mo :
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi GL
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo :
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Aut
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi T
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo →
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi Type
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{Conf}
                  \\coloneqq
                  \\vdash
                  \\prod_{D^n : \mathbf{B}GL(n)}
                  \\sum_{T\Sigma : \mathbf{B}\mathbf{Aut}(T\Sigma)}
                  T \Sigma \to GL(n)/O(n)   : Type
                  \\,,
          %p
            which is the integrated
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BRST+complex"} BRST complex
            of Einstein gravity field configurations modulo diffeomorphism ghosts: the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+infinity-groupoid"} smooth groupoid
            whose
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                are
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vielbein"} vielbein
                fields
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
                on
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
                are
              %ol
                %li
                  %p orthogonal frame transformations of the fibers of the tangent bundle;
                %li
                  %p
                    general diffeomorphisms of the base
                    = succeed "." do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi Σ
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
          %p We unwind this a bit more.
          %p A slight subtlety in interpreting the above expression is that in
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mi n
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi Type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  D^n : \mathbf{B}GL(n) \vdash \mathbf{B}Aut(T \Sigma) : Type
          %p
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+%E2%88%9E-group"} automorphism ∞-group
            of the tangent bundle it to be formed in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/context"} context
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}GL(n)
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+%E2%88%9E-group"} automorphism ∞-group
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}Aut(T \Sigma)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-image"} ∞-image
            of the name
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo *
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                  %mi Type
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi GL
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (* \stackrel{}{\to} Type) \in \mathbf{H}_{/\mathbf{B}GL(n)}
          %p
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Sigma \to \mathbf{B}GL(n))
            in the slice. By the discussion at
            %a{:href => "over-%28infinity%2C1%29-topos#ObjectClassifier"} slice-(∞,1)-topos – Object classifier
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object+classifier"} object classifier
            in the slice is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projection"} projection
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Type
                    %mo ×
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Type \times \mathbf{B}GL(n) \to \mathbf{B}GL(n))
          %p So the name and its pullback are given by a diagram of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Σ
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mi Type
                            %mo ^
                          %mo ×
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi GL
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
