          %h2#References References
          %h3#ReferencesHistory History
          %p The pre-history of the idea of general covariance is reviewed in
          %ul#Alexander
            %li
              H. G. Alexander (ed.),
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Leibniz-Clarke Correspondence: Together With Extracts from Newton’s Principia and Opticks
          %p
            The original articles by Einstein on the idea of general covariance include his
            %em Entwurf
            (sketch)
          %ul#EinsteinGrossmann
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Albert+Einstein"}> Albert Einstein
              , M. Grossmann,
              %em Entwurf einer verallgemeinerten Relativitätstheorie und einer Theorie der Gravitation
              Zeitschrift für Math. Phys. 62, 225–259 (1914)
          %p
            of the theory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            (where the notion of general covariance is still rejected) and then the full development of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+relativity"} general relativity
          %ul#Einstein1916
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Albert+Einstein"}> Albert Einstein
              ,
              %em Die Grundlage der allgemeinen Relativitätstheorie. Ann. Phys. (Leipzig) 49, 769–822 (1916)
          %p where it is fully embraced.
          %p An attempt at a fairly comprehensive review of the history of the idea of general covariance and its reception up to modern days is in
          %ul#Norton
            %li
              J. D. Norton,
              = succeed "," do
                %em General covariance and the foundations of general relativity: eight decades of dispute
              %strong 56
              (1993), (
              %a{:href => "http://www.pitt.edu/~jdnorton/papers/decades.pdf"}> original pdf
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.pitt.edu/~jdnorton/papers/decades_re-set.pdf"} reprint pdf
          %h3#ReferencesFormalizations Formalizations of general covariance
          %p
            A formalization in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AQFT"} AQFT
            is proposed and discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klaus+Fredenhagen"}> Klaus Fredenhagen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rudolf+Haag"} Rudolf Haag
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Generally covariant quantum field theory and scaling limits
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cmp/1104116359"} EUCLID
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Romeo+Brunetti"}> Romeo Brunetti
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klaus+Fredenhagen"} Klaus Fredenhagen
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rainer+Verch"} Rainer Verch
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The generally covariant locality principle – A new paradigm for local quantum physics
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math-ph/0112041"} math-ph/0112041
          %p A review is in
          %ul#BrunettiPorrmannRuzzi
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Romeo+Brunetti"}> Romeo Brunetti
              , Martin Porrmann, Giuseppe Ruzzi,
              %em General Covariance in Algebraic Quantum Field Theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math-ph/0512059"}> arXiv:math-ph/0512059
              )
          %p
            For more see the references at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AQFT+on+curved+spacetimes"} AQFT on curved spacetimes
          %p
            Via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+stacks"} quotient stacks
            in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-formalism"} BV-formalism
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Filip+Dul"}> Filip Dul
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %em General Covariance from the Viewpoint of Stacks
              %strong 113
              (2023) 30 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2112.15473"}> arXiv:2112.15473
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s11005-023-01653-3"} doi:10.1007/s11005-023-01653-3
          %h3#FormalizationInHomtopyTypeTheory Formalization in homotopy type theory
          %p
            Background and context for the above formalization of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+field+theory"} classical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            see
          %ul#SchreiberLectures
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+smooth+cohomology+in+string+theory"} twisted smooth cohomology in string theory
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://maths-old.anu.edu.au/esi/2012/"} ESI program on K-theory and quantum fields
              (2012)
          %ul#SchreiberShulman
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"} Mike Shulman
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Quantum+gauge+field+theory+in+Cohesive+homotopy+type+theory"} Quantum gauge field theory in Cohesive homotopy type theory
              (2012)
          %p
            See also
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory+and+physics"} higher category theory and physics
